{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>He ties his foal to the vine.</b> One of the signs of that king Messiah is that he will be revealed \"riding on a donkey, the colt of a she-ass,\" as the prophet says (Zechariah 9:9) — meaning he will not come upon a horse trained for the day of battle, for indeed the war of the nations and the destruction of their kingdoms will already have been completed by El, blessed be He, and he will be king in peace. Second, that he will tie that foal to the vine — meaning that the seat of his peaceful kingdom will dwell among Israel, who are likened to a vine, as the Sages, of blessed memory, said (Ḥullin 92a): \"This nation is likened to a vine\"; and the prophet likewise testified, saying: כִּי כֶרֶם ה' צְבָאוֹת בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל (Isaiah 5:7)." "<b>And to the choice vine, the son of his she-ass.</b> Third of his signs is that he will tether his donkey mentioned above, and his dwelling will be in the soreka, which is the choicest part of the vine — meaning he will turn his face toward the righteous of the generation, not toward the entire vine." "<b>He washes his garment in wine.</b> Fourth of his signs will be that he is able to wash his garment in blood, for much slaughter will have occurred before his arrival — as in ״מַדּוּעַ אָדוֹם לִלְבוּשֶׁךָ״ (Isaiah 63:2), and as it says: ״יָדִין בַּגּוֹיִם מָלֵא גְוִיּוֹת״ (Psalms 110:6)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:21.737333716Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}